E. The unit-cell cycles in the coordinate v = n + 1 (odd step: v -> 3v/2;
   even step: v -> (v+1)/2, so T_v = v(v+1)/2 = v * v')
==============================================================================
cell (1,0) D=+1  word 0  n-orbit [0]  v-orbit [1]
     v_bot = 1, v_top = 1, v_bot*v_top = 1, T_(v_top) = 1, 2^(k-1)*3^s = 1 = T_1
cell (1,1) D=-1  word 1  n-orbit [-1]  v-orbit [0]
     v_bot = 0, v_top = 0, v_bot*v_top = 0, T_(v_top) = 0, 2^(k-1)*3^s = 3 = T_2
cell (2,1) D=+1  word 10  n-orbit [1, 2]  v-orbit [2, 3]
     v_bot = 2, v_top = 3, v_bot*v_top = 6, T_(v_top) = 6, 2^(k-1)*3^s = 6 = T_3
