==============================================================================
F. One-halving circuits 1^a 0:  closes on an integer iff m*(2^(a+1) - 3^a) = 1
   (v_bot = m*2^a, v_top = m*3^a).  Equivalently 6^a is triangular.
==============================================================================
a <= 2000 with 6^a triangular: [0, 1, 2]  -> 6^a = [1, 6, 36]
a <= 2000 with |2^(a+1) - 3^a| = 1: [0, 1, 2]
(q odd in [3,1999], 1 <= a <= 60) with |2^(a+1) - q^a| = 1: [(3, 1, 1), (3, 2, -1), (5, 1, -1)]
  -> one-halving cycles: q=3,a=1 (cycle 1,2), q=3,a=2 (cycle -5,-7,-10), q=5,a=1 (cycle -1,-2).
  The only one with a >= 2 odd steps is (q, a) = (3, 2); its u-product is (2*3)^2 = 36 = T_8.
